# Docker ignores .gitignore entirely, so bin/ and obj/ — which git already ignores —
# were being uploaded to the daemon on every build: ~1.7 GB of context for a tree whose
# sources are a few MB.
#
# It is also a correctness fix, not only a speed one. Each Dockerfile restores first and
# then does `COPY services/<svc>/ services/<svc>/`, so a host obj/ folder lands on top of
# the restore output the image just produced — Windows absolute paths and a Windows RID
# graph overwriting the Linux one, inside a Linux container.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Editor/tooling state that has no bearing on a build.
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.user
**/TestResults/

# The build never reads these, and .git in particular is large.
.git/
**/*.md
